  [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m, so Node treats every [38;5;153m.js[39m file as CommonJS — which is what [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m rely on. A
  [38;5;153msrc/visitor-id.js[39m containing [38;5;153mexport[39m would therefore be fine in the browser but a syntax error under Node's test
  runner. Three ways out:

  - [1m[38;5;153msrc/visitor-id.mjs[0m — explicit ESM extension. Browser imports it identically; Node loads it as ESM; the two CommonJS
    files are untouched. Slight extension inconsistency.
  - [1mAdd [38;5;153m"type": "module"[0m — then [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m must be renamed to [38;5;153m.cjs[39m (plus a [38;5;153mmain[39m update), which drags
    unrelated files into this change.
  - [1mUse Vitest[0m — transpiles regardless of extension, at the cost of a real dependency and a config file.

  I recommend [1m[38;5;153m.mjs[0m. It's the only one that leaves the unrelated Node files alone, and the inconsistency disappears on
  its own if you later move the whole repo to ESM.

  [1mTest runner: [38;5;153mnode:test[39m + [38;5;153mnode:assert[39m, zero dependencies.[0m [38;5;153m"test": "node --test"[39m, tests in [38;5;153mtest/visitor-id.test.mjs[39m.
  This is where approach B pays off — every case below is a plain object literal standing in for storage:

  - empty storage → generates a UUID, writes it under [38;5;153mvisitorId[39m
  - second [38;5;153mget()[39m → same value, no second write
  - pre-populated storage → returns the stored value, doesn't overwrite
  - corrupt or empty stored value → replaces it with a fresh UUID
  - [38;5;153mgetItem[39m throws (private mode) → returns a usable ID, stable within the store
  - [38;5;153msetItem[39m throws (quota) → still returns a usable ID, doesn't propagate
  - across all of the above: never throws, never returns null

  [1mLint and format:[0m ESLint 9 flat config in [38;5;153meslint.config.mjs[39m with [38;5;153mjs.configs.recommended[39m, plus Prettier for formatting.
  Scripts: [38;5;153mlint[39m, [38;5;153mformat[39m. Both as devDependencies.

  [1mStatic server:[0m [38;5;153m"start": "serve ."[39m with [38;5;153mserve[39m as a devDependency, which is what makes the module script load.

  [1mNode version:[0m [38;5;153mcrypto.randomUUID()[39m is global from Node 19 on, so [38;5;153m"engines": { "node": ">=20" }[39m goes in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m to
  keep the tests honest about what they need.

  That's the whole design. Anything you want changed before I write it up as a spec?

